592186095272 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\sqrt[3]{6}cm" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095272 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095272 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ef522a1-0775-52d6-826e-a4a83a93e252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096588 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096588 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the volume of a sphere whose diameter is $18 \\:\\textrm{cm}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "012ce1ef-e254-5e9c-992b-e32d1e7c7043" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096588 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi r^3\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{18}{2}=9\\:\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi \\left(9\\right)^3 = 972\\pi \\:\\textrm{cm}^3\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096589 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096589 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the radius of a sphere whose volume is $36\\pi\\:\\textrm{in}^3$.\n\n![](images/99/99bb0ea67859fbd109442fcf698427ea43452087b4523b7202a760a2a8b27052.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f6bebf7-6276-5de9-8162-ea15a831f246" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096589 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi r^3\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nV=36\\pi\\:\\textrm{in}^3\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= \\frac{4}{3}πr^{3} \\\\\n36π &= \\frac{4}{3}πr^{3} \\\\\n36π \\cdot \\frac{3}{4π} &= r^{3} \\\\\nr^{3} &= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nr = \\sqrt[3]{27} = 3\\:\\textrm{in}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096779 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096779 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Volume of a Sphere Given Its Radius or Diameter" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096779 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096779 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "15868ae6-7843-5ae2-9fce-4d7b662f6763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096780 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096780 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Sphere Given Its Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096780 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096780 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7c5c224a-0c47-548b-a66f-101b03f6a4e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1045 "Volumes of Spheres" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096914 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8b72f1bb-5af6-54d1-9908-d6fc5cdc77fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097223 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186095267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097223 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32616" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097223 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/26/26b1e5acba63b8ee11d35e12bf0c8fd6944b7a466c9eab258ef36f6429e8ec0a.png)\n\nWhat is the radius of a sphere whose volume is $320πcm^{3}$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097223 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "91958ce6-c301-564b-89d6-6edfb21cb5a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097223 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097681 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097681 #edb/ref 1061 33643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097681 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ce10134-fed4-568d-af3e-a51e49129b8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097681 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097682 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097682 #edb/ref 1061 33644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097682 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c0a1895e-c996-52e0-b8b8-b53c41bb8e08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097682 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097683 #edb/ref 1061 33645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097683 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4d353c25-3da5-59b1-9654-280659b908c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097683 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097886 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a sphere with radius\n\n$$\nr= 3\\:\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\nhow do we calculate its volume?\n\n![](images/8d/8df0347cb30ac58b9cbcef4b7a7e25dfd35c899b1c833cdf2e8e22bcfc51971f.png)\n\nIn general, we can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV= \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi r^3\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nr=3\\:\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi \\cdot (3)^3 =36 \\pi \\:\\textrm{cm}^3\n$$\n\nWe often express the volume of a sphere as a multiple of $\\pi$. However, we can also use a calculator to get a numerical approximation. In this case, we get\n\n$$\nV \\approx 113.10 \\:\\textrm{cm}^3\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097886 #edb/ref 1065 5394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097886 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d15351c6-0d8b-5a7e-86b4-509daefe7cf5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097886 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
